{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci","id":1299855,"title":"Unique instruments, worth it? (and question about dropped foci)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-25T21:29:20-07:00","id":1299855,"title":"Unique instruments, worth it? (and question about dropped foci)","content":"In M20, a mage can choose an unique instrument for a sphere. It must be something very close to the mage and something that he is able to lose (some object), so it can't be praying, for example. Using an unique instrument grants a reduction of -1 in all Arete rolls made by that sphere. <br /> <br /> The price for that is: if the mage doesn't have his unique instrument when casting spells using that sphere he works as if &quot;Working without focus&quot;. Which means that the mage must spend a willpower point and make the Arete roll with +3 diff, in a pure act of Will. This also means that if a technomancer/technocrat loses his unique instrument, he cannot cast spells using that sphere anymore. If the unique instrument is destroyed, then your mage will have to cast without focus until raising his Arete enough to discard this instrument.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty high risk for just -1 on the Arete roll of one sphere. Do you think it's worth?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, M20 says that you can have more than one instrument for an effect as much as more than one effect using one instrument. So, let's say a Shaman that has blood, dance, drugs, voice, herbs ordeals and gems as instruments, and Arete 3 dropped the need to use his gems in his effects.<br /> And let's say that this shaman used Life 3 to get some bonus in strength. He did that by cutting his hand and covering part of his body in blood. <br /> Now he no longer needs his gems. If he cast this effect of raising strentgh using his blood and a gem (dropped) wouldn't he get the -1 diff bonus on the Arete roll?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T05:27:18-07:00","id":1299917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci#post1299855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And let's say that this shaman used Life 3 to get some bonus in strength. He did that by cutting his hand and covering part of his body in blood.<br /> Now he no longer needs his gems. If he cast this effect of raising strentgh using his blood and a gem (dropped) wouldn't he get the -1 diff bonus on the Arete roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>The bonus it's for actually using the instrument you dropped, not for casting a spell that normally would need that instrument with another instrument. He would gain the -1 if he actually uses a gem. That's a -2 if that gem was Unique, and the maximum of -3 if it's also Specialized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a pretty high risk for just -1 on the Arete roll of one sphere. Do you think it's worth? </div> </div> </div>As a powergaming choice, it's not a great choice. There are safer ways to get bonuses. It's not the worst choice ever, though: The item has to be something you can loose, but it doesn't need to be easy to break and mages can be pretty good finding stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T07:21:38-07:00","id":1299945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1299917#post1299917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The bonus it's for actually using the instrument you dropped, not for casting a spell that normally would need that instrument with another instrument. He would gain the -1 if he actually uses a gem. That's a -2 if that gem was Unique, and the maximum of -3 if it's also Specialized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. But you know, gems can be used mostly in any kind of effect. So the question is more like, could a mage fit a dropped instrument in conjunction with another that he used to use in order to improve his casting? <br /> In-game this means that the mage is increasing his focus. As I see, the more instruments a mage uses, more easily he focus on the casting.<br /> <br /> Out of game this means the -1 diff in Arete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a powergaming choice, it's not a great choice. There are safer ways to get bonuses. It's not the worst choice ever, though: The item has to be something you can loose, but it doesn't need to be easy to break and mages can be pretty good finding stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>What safer ways? Besides quintessence and unique/personal instruments, I don't see any other choice.<br /> Yes, mages can be good at finding stuff, but until then you lose the ability to cast spells from a whole sphere. If it is Correspondence, you're pretty much screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:07:03-07:00","id":1299957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1299945#post1299945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. But you know, gems can be used mostly in any kind of effect. So the question is more like, could a mage fit a dropped instrument in conjunction with another that he used to use in order to improve his casting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see why not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In-game this means that the mage is increasing his focus. As I see, the more instruments a mage uses, more easily he focus on the casting.<br /> <br /> Out of game this means the -1 diff in Arete. </div> </div> </div>Not quite, there's no advantage of using more than one Instrument unless you put a &quot;special&quot; instrument into the mix (specialized, unique, surpassed, or any combination). If you have a specialized instrument that's not unique and a unique instrument, you could combine them for a casting to get a -2. Otherwise it has no advantage.<br /> <br /> Also something to keep in mind: If you use those instruments for a spell, the ST could feel encouraged to ask for the same instruments when you cast it again (mandatory for a Rote). Hence you wouldn't be able to cast it w/o instruments until you've surpassed them all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What safer ways? Besides quintessence and unique/personal instruments, I don't see any other choice. </div> </div> </div>Well, you mentioned one. Many builds optimize their Quintessence gain/use. You could also try to build a useful Resonance to benefit more from your personal Quintessence<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> *Pulling Mythic Threads for a -1 can be as easy as the ST makes it to be. There are lots of legends, tropes and pop-culture feats to fuel your magick<br /> *A good Skill use implemented into your focus can reduce the difficulty too. A very good hit with &quot;violence as a focus&quot; cualifies, I think.<br /> *There are many Merits that reduce diff.<br /> <br /> As long as you avoid penalties a -3 it's optimal. Unique Specialized focuses are good to get a consistent -2, that's easy to transform in -3. But they have the disadvantages you mention to compensate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T09:39:02-07:00","id":1299980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci#post1299855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In M20, a mage can choose an unique instrument for a sphere. It must be something very close to the mage and something that he is able to lose (some object), so it can't be praying, for example. Using an unique instrument grants a reduction of -1 in all Arete rolls made by that sphere.<br /> <br /> The price for that is: if the mage doesn't have his unique instrument when casting spells using that sphere he works as if &quot;Working without focus&quot;. Which means that the mage must spend a willpower point and make the Arete roll with +3 diff, in a pure act of Will. This also means that if a technomancer/technocrat loses his unique instrument, he cannot cast spells using that sphere anymore. If the unique instrument is destroyed, then your mage will have to cast without focus until raising his Arete enough to discard this instrument.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty high risk for just -1 on the Arete roll of one sphere. Do you think it's worth?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, a Unique Instrument is unique because it can't be replaced, or would be very difficult to replace. Your grandfather's staff, after all, is unique. You could find one that was the same, but it wouldn't be your grandfather's. Same with a special violin or microscope.<br /> <br /> The bonus isn't that amazing when you consider that difficulty reductions exist all over the place in Mage. Specialized instruments are arguably much more effective, as they don't have this dependency linked to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-26-2019, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T09:44:52-07:00","id":1299982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1299957#post1299957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't see why not.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not quite, there's no advantage of using more than one Instrument unless you put a &amp;quot;special&amp;quot; instrument into the mix (specialized, unique, surpassed, or any combination). If you have a specialized instrument that's not unique and a unique instrument, you could combine them for a casting to get a -2. Otherwise it has no advantage.<br /> <br /> Also something to keep in mind: If you use those instruments for a spell, the ST could feel encouraged to ask for the same instruments when you cast it again (mandatory for a Rote). Hence you wouldn't be able to cast it w/o instruments until you've surpassed them all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, you mentioned one. Many builds optimize their Quintessence gain/use. You could also try to build a useful Resonance to benefit more from your personal Quintessence<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> *Pulling Mythic Threads for a -1 can be as easy as the ST makes it to be. There are lots of legends, tropes and pop-culture feats to fuel your magick<br /> *A good Skill use implemented into your focus can reduce the difficulty too. A very good hit with &amp;quot;violence as a focus&amp;quot; cualifies, I think.<br /> *There are many Merits that reduce diff.<br /> <br /> As long as you avoid penalties a -3 it's optimal. Unique Specialized focuses are good to get a consistent -2, that's easy to transform in -3. But they have the disadvantages you mention to compensate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes -3 is enough. I'll take a look at the merits. The skill only works for attacks. Unless you take more than 1 turn, in this case you could just take longer to cast and get the bonus, no need for skill roll.<br /> <br /> About the rote, the thing is, there are more than one way of casting the same effect. In the example, the shaman uses his blood to cast the effects, but I don't see why he couldn't add the gems too sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T11:35:30-07:00","id":1300016,"title":"","content":"O sure. You can use as many instruments as you feel appropiate, but it wouldn't count as a Rote if you change the Instrument. Rotes have fixed instruments (that means you may be fast-casting if you do it in a fight)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:55:55-07:00","id":1300073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300016#post1300016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O sure. You can use as many instruments as you feel appropiate, but it wouldn't count as a Rote if you change the Instrument. Rotes have fixed instruments (that means you may be fast-casting if you do it in a fight)</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, you don't have a limit for rotes either. The mage can drop the instrument and then begin using it (even creating new rotes with just this slight adjustment) to help focusing his effects.<br /> And fast casting is not casting without using a rote. Is castong without taking the necessary time do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T13:58:00-07:00","id":1300076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1299980#post1299980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, a Unique Instrument is unique because it can't be replaced, or would be very difficult to replace. Your grandfather's staff, after all, is unique. You could find one that was the same, but it wouldn't be your grandfather's. Same with a special violin or microscope.<br /> <br /> The bonus isn't that amazing when you consider that difficulty reductions exist all over the place in Mage. Specialized instruments are arguably much more effective, as they don't have this dependency linked to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that it cannot be replaced. It can be even dropped. The catch is the sentimental/spiritual value it has that really helps the mage focusing.<br /> <br /> And specialized instruments are only good for a few effects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T00:04:20-07:00","id":1300774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300076#post1300076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that it cannot be replaced. It can be even dropped. The catch is the sentimental/spiritual value it has that really helps the mage focusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough, though I'd argue that a mage's ability to drop particular Instruments is in inverse proportion to have dependent the mage is on that Instrument. On the grounds that heavily a relied upon Instrument turns into a spiritual crutch, stifling the mage's growing enlightenment (at least as far as that Instrument is concerned). Otherwise the player could use one Instrument for everything initially, then drop that Instrument at the first opportunity and never have to worry about them.<br /> <br /> If a mage uses a Unique Instrument often enough - and indeed because it's so useful and personally important to the mage - it gets overcome LAST. Unless the mage didn't use it that often in aggregate, or had a compelling role-play reason for why the Unique Instrument is suddenly not so vital.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And specialized instruments are only good for a few effects </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Sphere, and the Effects used from it. Forces has a high number of potent and varied applications, both offensive, defensive, and utilitarian.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the mage might only use a given Sphere for a single Effect. But that Effect might be really useful, or be employed really often. Time, especially, is known for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T01:58:47-07:00","id":1300781,"title":"","content":"Since there's a maximum -3 difficulty cap from the base difficulty, I feel like the bonus from a Unique instrument isn't really worth it. Node, as a background, is quite cheap. When you really need -3 difficulty you can throw 3 Quintessence at a problem. This is expensive but gets the job done.<br /> <br /> Now having a reliable -1 difficulty modifier is also a good idea, since it will save you a lot of Quintessence in the long run and ensures you do well on rolls where you wouldn't want to waste points. So that's where merits like Green Thumb and Hands of Daedalus come in handy. Green Thumb reduces the difficulty of most of the magick you use by 1 if you build your practice around plants/herbalism/fungi, and Hands of Daedalus turns basically anything you tinker with into a Personalized instrument, meaning you're at -1 difficulty to use magick with almost all of your possessions as long as you invest in the Craft/Tech/Hypertech/Computer necessary to tinker with and tweak them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T02:53:04-07:00","id":1300783,"title":"","content":"Do not underestimate, however, cases where the difficulty is *higher* than base.<br /> Somebody with an unique instrument - even more so when it is by then Specialized, or the effect requires none but they still use it, or if they have one of the merits you mentioned - can essentially drop a +3 situation back to base for free, and then just slam 3 quintessence into it; Pretty much turning a +3 moment into -3 on the fly. That is quite quite powerful, especially since they only use 3 quint total to do so.<br /> <br /> Naturally most of that is possible with Avatar 5 and popping 5 quint in, but that is...quite expensive to do, and I feel that the Avatar rating, especially at 4 to 5, has a big influence on the character's overall naration, behavior and everyday life. Powerful Avatars are a scary thing to have, and not always something the character enjoys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-29-2019, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T04:14:03-07:00","id":1300798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300783#post1300783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not underestimate, however, cases where the difficulty is *higher* than base.<br /> Somebody with an unique instrument - even more so when it is by then Specialized, or the effect requires none but they still use it, or if they have one of the merits you mentioned - can essentially drop a +3 situation back to base for free, and then just slam 3 quintessence into it; Pretty much turning a +3 moment into -3 on the fly. That is quite quite powerful, especially since they only use 3 quint total to do so.<br /> <br /> Naturally most of that is possible with Avatar 5 and popping 5 quint in, but that is...quite expensive to do, and I feel that the Avatar rating, especially at 4 to 5, has a big influence on the character's overall naration, behavior and everyday life. Powerful Avatars are a scary thing to have, and not always something the character enjoys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely worth keeping in mind yes. It's just that there are a LOT of ways to reduce difficulty in Mage, and picking one that hampers you like a Unique instrument (meaning you're really in trouble without it for certain effects) could be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> I think the &quot;Best&quot; solution is to take Enchanting feature. Unique specialized instrument that you always have with you. Best of both worlds, very cheap merit, also makes a tonne of mundane rolls way easier (removing the need to even use magick in a lot of situations).<br /> <br /> A question about modifiers though; if there are +5 worth of difficulty modifiers (fast-casting, reversing time, distracted) to an effect, and you get -2 difficulty modification, does it turn from +3 into +1 difficulty, or +3 into +3? Essentially do the &quot;extra&quot; difficulty increases hang around making it harder to simplify the effect with Quintessence and similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-29-2019, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T04:58:12-07:00","id":1300802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300798#post1300798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about modifiers though; if there are +5 worth of difficulty modifiers (fast-casting, reversing time, distracted) to an effect, and you get -2 difficulty modification, does it turn from +3 into +1 difficulty, or +3 into +3? Essentially do the &quot;extra&quot; difficulty increases hang around making it harder to simplify the effect with Quintessence and similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>It turns +3 into +3. The -3/+3 limit applies at the end of the equation.<br /> <br /> Something Mind users should have in mind (anything too forced it's already at +3, plus another +3 if it's against a supernatural. You would need a -6 to diff to cast at normal diff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T06:12:37-07:00","id":1300812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300802#post1300802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It turns +3 into +3. The -3/+3 limit applies at the end of the equation.<br /> <br /> Something Mind users should have in mind (anything too forced it's already at +3, plus another +3 if it's against a supernatural. You would need a -6 to diff to cast at normal diff).</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the +3 limit didn't apply to those Willpower-based difficulties? I only say that because the examples talk about +5 difficulty totals, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And yes if someone has Willpower 9 and is a supernatural being, it's difficulty 12 for starters, possibly difficulty 15 if you're doing &quot;DANCE PUPPETS DANCE&quot; style magick. But my question would be does the +3 cap actually apply here?<br /> <br /> But knowing that -3/+3 cap is applied at the end of the equation is very helpful, thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T07:37:28-07:00","id":1300833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300812#post1300812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the +3 limit didn't apply to those Willpower-based difficulties? I only say that because the examples talk about +5 difficulty totals, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And yes if someone has Willpower 9 and is a supernatural being, it's difficulty 12 for starters, possibly difficulty 15 if you're doing &quot;DANCE PUPPETS DANCE&quot; style magick. But my question would be does the +3 cap actually apply here?<br /> <br /> But knowing that -3/+3 cap is applied at the end of the equation is very helpful, thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. My take it's that Willpower-based difficulties supersede the usual limits on difficulty modifiers <b><u>only </u></b>in regards to the +3/+5 you get for trying to use Mind on nightfolk.<br /> <br /> This superseding it's only mentioned in the &quot;Mind-Mages and Night-Folk&quot; section as an exception: &quot;Yes, this supersedes the usual limits on difficulty modifiers, and yes it makes it very hard to force Night-Folk to perform acts they are not willing to perform.&quot; There's no other instance where a +5 to diff it's discussed, except in regards to <i>sleepers </i>performing social conditioning w/o magick.<br /> <br /> Other difficulty modifiers are never mentioned as superseding the usual rules, and thus one could argue that these don't supersede the usual rules. Hence the maximum diff for forcing a mortal to do something he doesn't want to would be +3, and for nightfolk +8","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-29-2019, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T07:54:53-07:00","id":1300840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300774#post1300774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough, though I'd argue that a mage's ability to drop particular Instruments is in inverse proportion to have dependent the mage is on that Instrument. On the grounds that heavily a relied upon Instrument turns into a spiritual crutch, stifling the mage's growing enlightenment (at least as far as that Instrument is concerned). Otherwise the player could use one Instrument for everything initially, then drop that Instrument at the first opportunity and never have to worry about them.<br /> <br /> If a mage uses a Unique Instrument often enough - and indeed because it's so useful and personally important to the mage - it gets overcome LAST. Unless the mage didn't use it that often in aggregate, or had a compelling role-play reason for why the Unique Instrument is suddenly not so vital.<br /> <br /> <br /> Depends on the Sphere, and the Effects used from it. Forces has a high number of potent and varied applications, both offensive, defensive, and utilitarian.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the mage might only use a given Sphere for a single Effect. But that Effect might be really useful, or be employed really often. Time, especially, is known for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since you can have any number of rotes and use amy number of instruments in your casting you could simply start using your sropped instrument in your effects, considering it is generic enough.<br /> I gave an example where the mage doesn't used gems in much effects. After dropping it first (because he didn't used a lot) he began to implement it into his effects. He stilk needs the blood to buff his strength, but now he realised that using the gem in conjunction makes he focus better. He couldn't do it without blood, because he still think it is necessary, since it is his primary instrument.<br /> <br /> And still, specialized instruments don't cover all effects like a a personalised (or maybe unique) do. And they need a very good explanation too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T07:59:18-07:00","id":1300841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300798#post1300798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the &amp;quot;Best&amp;quot; solution is to take Enchanting feature. Unique specialized instrument that you always have with you. Best of both worlds, very cheap merit, also makes a tonne of mundane rolls way easier (removing the need to even use magick in a lot of situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this applies to allthe effects using, voice movement, etc? Or just the ones where the mage is trying to seduce (or any social effect)?<br /> <br /> Also, tsking those kind of merit means that the mage cannot have a normal unique/personalised instru?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T08:10:56-07:00","id":1300845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300841#post1300841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this applies to allthe effects using, voice movement, etc? Or just the ones where the mage is trying to seduce (or any social effect)?<br /> <br /> Also, tsking those kind of merit means that the mage cannot have a normal unique/personalised instru?</div> </div> </div> </div>So take Enchanting Feature, Voice. It would reduce the difficulty of all rolls reasonable helped by it Art (Singing, Poetry, Rap), Expression, Leadership, Seduction, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> It would also reduce the difficulty of magick where you made your voice the instrument. So mind control via speech, for example. This counts as a Unique/Personalised instrument modifier.<br /> <br /> And I don't know actually. I believe you can take the merit multiple times though. So a Mage whose whole thing was being a pop icon could take Voice, Eyes, Physique, costing 6 freebies and meaning they get -2 difficulty to the following Instruments: Incantations and Vocalizations, Eye Contact, Dance and Movements / Fashion / Sex and Sensuality.<br /> <br /> Honestly on one hand I'd love to play a Mage who is kinda dumb but has Fame 4, jaw-dropping looks and an enormous cult (heh) following, with these sorts of merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T08:14:43-07:00","id":1300846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300841#post1300841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this applies to allthe effects using, voice movement, etc? Or just the ones where the mage is trying to seduce (or any social effect)?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the effects where your &quot;feature&quot; could be justified as part of the Focus. Social effects are an obvious choice, but there's no need to limit it to social effects - For instance, someone who has, literally, the voice of an angel could be better equiped to chant in their language (hermetic focus) than someone with a normal larynx (hence hurl better fireballs)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, tsking those kind of merit means that the mage cannot have a normal unique/personalised instru? </div> </div> </div>If the Merit doesn't say so, it doesn't limit your mage in any special way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T08:33:36-07:00","id":1300849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300846#post1300846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the effects where your &quot;feature&quot; could be justified as part of the Focus. Social effects are an obvious choice, but there's no need to limit it to social effects - For instance, someone who has, literally, the voice of an angel could be better equiped to chant in their language (hermetic focus) than someone with a normal larynx (hence hurl better fireballs)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It could be argued it's an overpowered merit in fact! But it is mitigated by the fact that the merit draws negative attention towards the &quot;source of your power&quot;. The mage whose words are like honey is the one who will be gagged first, in the same way that the mage who is an Absolute Unit (7 foot tall, made of muscle) will be the first one they tranquilize and put restraints on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:02:28-07:00","id":1300896,"title":"","content":"The merit description is pretty clear that any of those practices listed (voice, dance and movement, ordeals, etc.) get the bonus. It's similar to the green thumb merit, tou don't have to take the merit for every kind of herb or plant, you get the bonus for using all the listed instruments.<br /> Now, I don't know if you would get the bonus for all effects that use those instruments. According to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> an hermetic could use his powerful voice to cast a fireball better than the others.<br /> Then you could also buff your physical abilities with Life by working out, since it includes ordeal, am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:24:50-07:00","id":1300902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300896#post1300896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you could also buff your physical abilities with Life by working out, since it includes ordeal, am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, if you have the body of Adonis to be super strong comes with the territory. Your beautiful muscles channel excersise better than most","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T14:20:28-07:00","id":1300945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300896#post1300896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merit description is pretty clear that any of those practices listed (voice, dance and movement, ordeals, etc.) get the bonus. It's similar to the green thumb merit, tou don't have to take the merit for every kind of herb or plant, you get the bonus for using all the listed instruments.<br /> Now, I don't know if you would get the bonus for all effects that use those instruments. According to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> an hermetic could use his powerful voice to cast a fireball better than the others.<br /> Then you could also buff your physical abilities with Life by working out, since it includes ordeal, am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd only take the merit multiple times if you wanted a broad range of options yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T23:06:48-07:00","id":1301038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1300945#post1300945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd only take the merit multiple times if you wanted a broad range of options yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You saying that you could take only one practice? Then it wouldn't work as green thumb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T05:31:50-07:00","id":1301586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1301038#post1301038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You saying that you could take only one practice? Then it wouldn't work as green thumb?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works with as many Practices as you want, but you need to get into the spirit of the Merit. An angelical voice isn't going to allow you to increase your muscle mass with &quot;ordeals&quot; because an angelical voice has no place as such an Instrument.<br /> <br /> You may, perhaps, Sing to your muscles into growing (if your mage it's crazy enought tn believe that could work), but it ain't going to help Instruments that don't involve singing or talking or, you know, <i>using your angelical voice</i>.<br /> <br /> The general idea it's that you have one &quot;special trait&quot; that could be used as an Instrument if it makes sense to use it as an Instrument. Your M20 experience it's going to be much happier if instead of trying to find ways to game the system you try to follow it's spirit (as described by the fluff).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T05:53:34-07:00","id":1301590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1301586#post1301586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works with as many Practices as you want, but you need to get into the spirit of the Merit. An angelical voice isn't going to allow you to increase your muscle mass with &quot;ordeals&quot; because an angelical voice has no place as such an Instrument.<br /> <br /> You may, perhaps, Sing to your muscles into growing (if your mage it's crazy enought tn believe that could work), but it ain't going to help Instruments that don't involve singing or talking or, you know, <i>using your angelical voice</i>.<br /> <br /> The general idea it's that you have one &quot;special trait&quot; that could be used as an Instrument if it makes sense to use it as an Instrument. Your M20 experience it's going to be much happier if instead of trying to find ways to game the system you try to follow it's spirit (as described by the fluff).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this exactly. People should use the instruments that make sense. Summoning Angels and Banishing Demons with your angelic voice and hymns? Amazingly good fit. A soothing song and heals those who hear it? Perfect, and the same would work for mental/spiritual healing. But using singing to strengthen and tone your own muscles is a good example of where such a benefit doesn't really make sense.<br /> <br /> Basically the ST should just say when they think a character is using the wrong instrument, and they can always try and justify or tweak it. &quot;Well how about he isn't using a song to cross the gauntlet... what if I try and weaken the gauntlet before I cross over, using heavenly chanting?&quot; &quot;Okay, so it doesn't make sense for him to knock the guard out with his voice... but could we say that his soothing heavenly singing causes the guard to drift to sleep?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T07:44:51-07:00","id":1301622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1299855-unique-instruments-worth-it-and-question-about-dropped-foci?p=1301586#post1301586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works with as many Practices as you want, but you need to get into the spirit of the Merit. An angelical voice isn't going to allow you to increase your muscle mass with &amp;quot;ordeals&amp;quot; because an angelical voice has no place as such an Instrument.<br /> <br /> You may, perhaps, Sing to your muscles into growing (if your mage it's crazy enought tn believe that could work), but it ain't going to help Instruments that don't involve singing or talking or, you know, <i>using your angelical voice</i>.<br /> <br /> The general idea it's that you have one &amp;quot;special trait&amp;quot; that could be used as an Instrument if it makes sense to use it as an Instrument. Your M20 experience it's going to be much happier if instead of trying to find ways to game the system you try to follow it's spirit (as described by the fluff).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that the merit allowed more than one feature, and that any instrument in the list would get the bonus just like &quot;hand of daedalus&quot;. <br /> <br /> Also, having a &quot;strong and gracefull body&quot; covers almost all of the instruments in the list..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}